text:
Proof is not routine in one step.

What `td0_exec_potential_le` needs:
* per-side update lemma: `accrueSide` converts `unindexed` into `pending` with floor-division loss, so scaled potential `doubleScale*credited+pending+doubleScale*unindexed` does not rise;
* per-side distribute lemma: settling one account converts its `pendingAcct` into `accrued` with floor-division loss, list `sum` does not rise;
* `grant` only moves `accrued` to `wallet`, `credited` unchanged;
* `advance k` raises potential by exactly `doubleScale*k*(sp.1+sp.2)`;
* balance-change ops happen only after the affected account was settled to the new index, so they create no new `pending`; `setSpeeds`/`claim`/`transfer` (two hooks) compose the above;
* `td0_Inv` (blocks not ahead, recorded indices ≤ market indices, speeds = ghost speeds) to discharge side-conditions and `emittedBy` case split.

No single `omega`/`simp` closes the division-rounding plus `List.sum` reasoning; it must be split into the per-side/per-op lemmas above.

